---
// The standing home of the three-way condominium comparison.
//
// It exists as a page and not only as a figure inside one article because the tool is general and
// the article is not: someone weighing two blocks in Serangoon has no reason to read a piece about
// a launch in Bishan. On this page the opening three are left to the component's own default —
// the most-traded buildings in the data — so the page starts with no local bias.
//
// What this page must never become: a ranking. The component reports leaders only on the three
// measures that have a direction, refuses to score the four that do not, and adds nothing up. The
// copy here has to hold that line too, because a standalone tool page is exactly where a "best
// condo in Singapore" framing would creep in.
import MainLayout from '@src/layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import CondoCompare from '@src/components/CondoCompare.astro';
import CategoryWidget from '@src/components/CategoryWidget.astro';
import FeaturedPostWidget from '@src/components/FeaturedPostWidget.astro';
import TagsWidget from '@src/components/TagsWidget.astro';
import { Icon } from 'astro-icon/components';
import { url } from '@src/utils/path';

const title = 'Compare Three Singapore Condominiums on the Public Record';
const description =
  'Put any three of 309 Singapore condominiums side by side on median resale price, how often ' +
  'units change hands, lease remaining, the walk to a station, the size that actually trades, ' +
  'and where each sits against its own district. Free, computed from URA and LTA records, and ' +
  'deliberately unscored.';

const DATA_ASOF = 'August 2026';
const VERIFIED = '8 August 2026';

const site = Astro.site ?? new URL('https://theenoughpoint.com');
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: title,
  description,
  url: new URL('/condo-compare/', site).href,
  applicationCategory: 'FinanceApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any',
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'SGD' },
  inLanguage: 'en-SG',
  isPartOf: { '@type': 'WebSite', name: 'TheEnoughPoint', url: site.href },
};
---

<MainLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />

  <div class="container xl:max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 flex flex-col gap-4 lg:gap-6">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4 lg:gap-6 py-6">
      <div class="max-lg:mb-12 lg:col-span-2 py-4">
        <h1 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-heading font-bold text-navy py-4">
          Compare three condominiums, on the public record
        </h1>

        <div class="pb-4 w-full flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-sm text-muted border-b border-cream-dark">
          <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <Icon name="bi:calendar" class="size-3.5" />
            Data to {DATA_ASOF} · checked {VERIFIED}
          </span>
          <a href={url('/author/fi')} rel="author" class="flex items-center gap-1.5 hover:text-brand-600">
            <Icon name="bi:person" class="size-3.5" />
            FI
          </a>
          <a href={url('/build-enough')} class="flex items-center gap-1.5 hover:text-brand-600">
            <Icon name="bi:bookmark" class="size-3.5" />
            Build Enough
          </a>
        </div>

        <div class="relative post-content pt-6">
          <p>Property listings will tell you a building is well connected, well held and well
          priced. The public record can actually check two of those, and it is free.</p>

          <p>This puts any three condominiums side by side on seven measures drawn from URA
          transaction data and LTA station locations: what units there actually resell for, how
          often they change hands, how much lease is left, how far the nearest station really is,
          the size that genuinely trades, the typical price paid, and where each sits against
          same-size resale in its own district.</p>

          <CondoCompare />

          <h2>Why there is no winner at the bottom</h2>

          <p>Because three of these seven measures have a better end and four of them do not, and
          adding the two kinds together would be arithmetic pretending to be judgement.</p>

          <p>More lease is more lease. More resales mean an easier exit. A shorter walk is a
          shorter walk. Those three have a direction, so the tool marks who leads and by how far.
          But a higher price per square foot is good news for an owner and bad news for a buyer.
          A larger typical unit suits one household and not the next. Sitting above your district
          can mean a newer block, a higher floor or a shorter walk just as easily as it can mean
          paying up. There is no honest way to score those without deciding, on your behalf, what
          you want &mdash; so the tool reports them and stops.</p>

          <h2>What it cannot see</h2>

          <p>A median is a median. It mixes the ground-floor unit facing the car park with the
          high floor facing the reserve, and the one renovated last year with the one untouched
          since handover. Two buildings can differ on this page for reasons that have nothing to
          do with either building.</p>

          <p>It also only covers the liquid end of the market. A project appears only if at least
          ten units resold in the last twelve months, which 309 of roughly 1,135 condominiums
          manage. Below that a median moves on a single unusual sale, and a number resting on two
          transactions is worse than no number. If a building you are considering is missing, that
          is usually why &mdash; and the thinness is itself worth knowing before you buy into it.</p>

          <p>Nothing here is a recommendation, a valuation or a forecast, and no building on this
          page is being put forward as a good or bad buy. It is a free reading of what the public
          record says, so you can arrive at a viewing with the checkable part already checked.</p>

          <div class="post-notes">
            <p class="note-aside">A note on what this is not. We are not recommending any
            development, district or developer, and we take no view on whether property belongs in
            anyone's plan. Buildings are named because a comparison tool is useless without names,
            and every figure carries its source and the number of sales behind it. We build a free
            Singapore property decision tool, sell no property, mortgages or advice, carry no
            advertising, and earn nothing from any link on this page.</p>

            <p class="note-legal">General information and education only. This is not financial,
            mortgage or tax advice and takes no account of your objectives, situation or needs.
            Property is illiquid and its transaction costs are large. Transaction records are
            revised and medians move; check current figures at their primary source before relying
            on anything here.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="lg:col-span-1 flex flex-col gap-6 py-4">
        <CategoryWidget />
        <FeaturedPostWidget />
        <TagsWidget />
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</MainLayout>
